<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Gold Fields Namibia names Robinson new head.</title>
<headline>Gold Fields Namibia names Robinson new head.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold Fields Namibia Ltd said on Wednesday that it had appointed Hugh Robinson to be its new managing director from April 1.</p>
<p>Robinson has been the managing partner in Namibia for accounting and consulting firm Ernst &amp; Young since 1985.</p>
<p>The firm also said that production at its Kombat copper mine was being limited to the No. 3 Shaft as flood water is still being pumped out of the other sections of the mine.</p>
<p>Kombat was one mine damaged during a bitter wages strike at Gold Fields Namibia's Tsumeb Corp Ltd unit in the second half of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
